A solution is 5\% in mass and its solute has a MW of 150g/mol. Calculate:
\begin{inparaenum}[(a)]
\item the mole fraction of the solution if it's a water-based solution  % $6\times 10^{-3}$
\item the mole fraction of the solution if it's an ethanol-based solution and ethanol's MW is  32g/mol % 0.01
\end{inparaenum} 
